<edge source="iran_gulf_offensive::energy_shipment_flow" target="ai_tech_power_shift::ai_investment_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">A drop in energy shipment flow raises regional/global energy prices and operating costs for cloud and data‑center operators, prompting investors and corporate treasuries to reduce or reprioritize capital allocated to AI R&amp;D and startups.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_gulf_offensive</data>
  <data key="d40">ai_tech_power_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_gulf_offensive::energy_shipment_flow" target="global_monetary_tighteni::policy_rate_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher energy shipment flows relieve upward pressure on global fuel prices and inflation expectations, reducing central banks' impetus to raise policy interest rates, whereas disrupted/reduced flows push rates up to counter inflation.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_gulf_offensive</data>
  <data key="d40">global_monetary_tighteni</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_gulf_offensive::energy_shipment_flow" target="russia_west_confrontatio::energy_vulnerability" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.75</data>
  <data key="d37">Lowered petroleum/fuel shipments from the Gulf shrink spare global capacity and raise price volatility, directly increasing energy supply vulnerability for Western consumers and changing leverage dynamics in the Russia–West energy dimension.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_gulf_offensive</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_west_confrontatio</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_gulf_offensive::energy_shipment_flow" target="us_china_strategic_rival::policy_uncertainty" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Intermittent or reduced oil and fuel shipments from the Gulf create volatile import flows and price risk for Chinese industry and traders, raising uncertainty about future regulatory and trade responses between U.S. and China and complicating corporate planning.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_gulf_offensive</data>
  <data key="d40">us_china_strategic_rival</data>
</edge>
