  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Higher U.S.–China trade barriers incentivize China to lock in larger, long‑term energy purchases from Russia to secure supply chains, strengthening Russia's alternative markets and reducing Western leverage over Russian export decisions, which increases Western energy supply vulnerability.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_strategic_rival</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_west_confrontatio</data>
</edge>
