<edge source="us_china_strategic_rival::policy_uncertainty" target="ai_tech_power_shift::model_deployment_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Heightened unpredictability about future rules and enforcement causes firms to postpone or scale back deployments and pilots of models to avoid compliance risk and potential market disruptions.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_strategic_rival</data>
  <data key="d40">ai_tech_power_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_strategic_rival::policy_uncertainty" target="global_monetary_tighteni::investor_risk_appetite" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising unpredictability about future US–China regulatory, sanction or tariff moves raises the probability of sudden losses, prompting investors to reduce allocations to risky assets and de‑leverage.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_strategic_rival</data>
  <data key="d40">global_monetary_tighteni</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_china_strategic_rival::policy_uncertainty" target="russia_west_confrontatio::corporate_exposure" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.55</data>
  <data key="d37">Acute unpredictability in U.S.–China policy prompts multinationals to hastily reorganize supply chains, legal entities and on‑the‑ground operations (including expanding local footprints or intermediated relationships), which raises their legal, financial and operational exposure to Russia‑West confrontation measures such as sanctions or asset restrictions.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_china_strategic_rival</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_west_confrontatio</data>
</edge>
