<edge source="global_monetary_tighteni::gov_bond_yield_curve" target="ai_tech_power_shift::ai_capability_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising long-term sovereign yields increase the financing cost of multi-year capex (data centers, specialized hardware), prompting firms to delay or scale back large compute-intensive training runs and slowing near-term gains in aggregate AI capability.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_monetary_tighteni</data>
  <data key="d40">ai_tech_power_shift</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_monetary_tighteni::gov_bond_yield_curve" target="iran_gulf_offensive::maritime_accessibility" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.55</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained upward pressure across the sovereign yield curve raises government debt servicing costs, forcing near‑term budgetary cuts or delayed spending on coastguard patrols, port security and maritime infrastructure, reducing safe commercial access through chokepoints.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_monetary_tighteni</data>
  <data key="d40">iran_gulf_offensive</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_monetary_tighteni::gov_bond_yield_curve" target="russia_west_confrontatio::alliance_cohesion" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">A sustained upward shift in sovereign yields (especially among key European allies) tightens domestic fiscal space and raises political and budgetary costs of sustained sanctions or military assistance, producing pressure for policy divergence and weakening alliance cohesion.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">global_monetary_tighteni</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_west_confrontatio</data>
</edge>
